Repository License And Provenance Boundary

Copyright (c) 2017-2026 David M. Levinson, Bernard Marion, Andrew Owen,
Mengying Cui, and repository contributors

This repository is a mixed research package. The license below applies only
to materials that the paper authors or repository maintainers have rights to
license, and it does not relicense publication PDFs, provider-governed public
data, public-agency GIS layers, source geometry, vendor file-format
structures, or third-party materials.

## Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International

Author-created repository documentation, package metadata, source-decision
notes, data dictionaries, manifests, and rights-cleared derived package
metadata are licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
International License (CC BY 4.0):

https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/4.0/

This license also covers author-created derived accessibility tables,
person-weighted accessibility summaries, standard-deviational-ellipse change
metrics, and map-ready accessibility/decomposition outputs in the staged
workbooks and GIS attributes only to the extent they consist of
author-created selection, cleaning, integration, calculations, or analysis
controlled by the paper authors or repository maintainers.

## Materials Not Relicensed

This repository license does not apply to:

- The publication PDF under `paper/`, which retains its publisher,
  repository, or manuscript terms.
- US Census, LEHD, CTPP, MnDOT, Metropolitan Council, loop-detector,
  traffic-count, TAZ, highway, public-agency, or other upstream/source data.
- Metropolitan Council GIS data, GIS geometry, source boundaries, highway
  layers, source notices, or derivative portions that must retain the
  Metropolitan Council GIS disclaimer. The staged disclaimer in
  `data/gis/cif-shapes/notice.rtf` must remain with transmitted GIS data or
  derivative portions when applicable.
- TransCAD, ArcGIS/QGIS, Microsoft Excel, LibreOffice, shapefile, geodatabase,
  SQLite, or other vendor/runtime/file-format structures and application
  metadata.
- Drafts, review letters, submission files, cited references, and other
  third-party or externally controlled materials.

## Software Boundary

No executable software, scripts, notebooks, model source code, matrix-
construction scripts, accessibility calculation scripts, or paper-specific
runtime code are staged in this repository. This root license therefore
grants no separate software license.
